METHODOLOGY CORRECTION — read this before trusting the states 1-2 block above.
The prior handoff instructed: "use /api/status fps as the detach oracle — it
collapses when the preview GL context detaches." BOTH HALVES ARE WRONG:
  * The route is /api/health. /api/status returns EMPTY on port 8080.
  * fps does NOT collapse on detach. It is stored at exactly one site,
    Renderer.cpp:181, inside renderOpenGL(). When the context detaches the
    callback stops, so the last value PERSISTS INDEFINITELY. Measured live this
    session: with the context PROVABLY dead, fps reported 106.18.
  * The 2.4e-06 reading in the states 1-2 block above is NOT a detach. fpsTimer_
    initialises to 0.0 and JUCE's hi-res counter is ms-since-boot, so the first
    frame computes 1/uptime. 1/2.403e-06 = 416,090s = 4.82 days. Nothing to read
    into it. State 1 re-measured this session: steady 108-118 fps.

